Encompasses: stolen operational service tokens, legitimate API abuse, internal privilege escalation, authorized channel exploitation, lateral cloud traversal.
  Vulnerability: Hardware-enforced attestation, continuous behavioral anomaly detection, and cryptographically bound ephemeral tokens can restrict identity delegation so narrowly that credential theft does not grant lateral movement outside an isolated enclave.
